## 2. Script — script.md
- 153 words, 10 segments, hook -> what -> categories -> sign-in -> enter ->
  grading -> sealed -> paid -> why -> CTA "aiprove.fun".
- Decisions (builder's, per brief): landscape 1920x1080 (any style allowed);
  30fps (spec minimum; 60fps would double render time with no visible gain on
  slow flat-vector motion); no music bed (VO only, clean); scene-level captions
  (segment's own words, dark box, max 2 lines, held per segment — no flicker).

## 3. VO — /opt/hatch/bin/tts (Helio voice avocado_v2:MAI_03, speed 100)
- First attempt: pip-installed edge-tts, but its aiohttp TLS fails through the
  sandbox egress proxy (SSL WRONG_VERSION_NUMBER to speech.platform.bing.com).
  Fell back to the built-in /opt/hatch/bin/tts.
- Speed 78 test: 16 words in 6.07s (2.64 w/s) — too slow for 60s target.
- Speed 80: total 73.18s — too long (sentence-boundary pauses add up).
- Speed 100 (final): per-segment durations s01 4.848, s02 5.232, s03 5.232,
  s04 7.152, s05 4.320, s06 7.440, s07 5.808, s08 6.600, s09 5.472, s10 7.008
  = 59.112s total.
- Pronunciation note: TTS input used "AI Prove" (spaced) and "AI Prove dot fun"
  so the brand name is spoken as letters, matching the written script.
- Verification: faster-whisper (small model) transcription of the concatenated
  VO — all 153 words present; "keypair" heard as "key pair", "AIProve" heard as
  "AI Prove" (same spoken words). VO complete, no clipping.

## 4. Audio assembly
- First concat attempt (mixed mp3 + 48kHz wav) silently dropped the 0.1s
  silence gaps (59.112s, mp3 decode errors in stderr). Redone properly:
  all segments converted to 48kHz stereo wav first, then concat with 0.1s
  silence between segments = 60.012s.
- loudnorm I=-16:TP=-1:LRA=11 (linear) -> audio/vo-60-norm.wav, 60.012s.

## 5. Video render — render.py (PIL, original flat-vector graphics)
- 10 scenes, one per VO segment; scene timing follows measured VO + 0.1s gaps.
  Palette: navy #0E1B2E, teal #2AB7A0, gold #F2B705, orange #F08A3C, cream.
  No AI-generated images/video used (code-drawn only, avoids the bounty's
  generated-footage transcript check). Poster art used as palette/motif
  reference only — everything redrawn.
- Test frames rendered for all 10 scenes and visually checked. Fixes made:
  (a) scene 0: gold coin overlapped the subtitle and the robot's body was
  partly hidden behind the caption box -> moved text up, robot/coin up;
  (b) scene 7: STOCK/ETH/PROVE chips half-hidden behind the caption box ->
  moved chips up 40px.
- Full render: 1800 frames (30fps, 60.0s) in 4 parallel chunks (0-450,
  450-900, 900-1350, 1350-1800). Chunk 450-900 FAILED at frame 852:
  ValueError in PIL rounded_rectangle — the AutoGrade meter fill bar width
  (~41.5px) fell just under 2*radius+2 (42px). Fixed with a guard (rounded
  rect only when width >= 44px, plain rect below that) + same guard for the
  wordmark underline. Re-rendered frames 852-899. Final count: 1800 frames.
- Encode: ffmpeg image sequence -> libx264 CRF 18, yuv420p, faststart;
  muxed with vo-60-norm.wav trimmed to 60.0s, AAC 192k.

